  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1221 AM CST Sat Nov 28 2026\n\nThere are few changes in the thinking for the for long term\nforecast from the previous issuance amd that long term section\nis included below.\n\nMuch of next week looks to feature semi- zonal flow \ntransitioning to southwest flow aloft late Wednesday into \nThursday. This will lead toward a warming trend well above \nnormal, as we go through the first week of meteorological winter\n(CPC probabilities of above normal temperatures at 80-90% Dec \n2-6). In fact high temperatures on Wednesday and Thursday will \nbe in the mid to upper 50s area wide. The peak of this warming \nshould arrive mid- week as the flow turns southwest ahead of \nsystem ejecting from the desert southwest. This system will \nbring our next chance of precipitation late in the week, and \ngiven that southwest systems tend to slow I wouldn't be \nsurprised to see PoPs come down more for Thursday and increase \non Friday. Given the lack of cold air with this storm system \nrain and wind would be the primary impacts, but we'd also need \nto keep an eye on the thunderstorm potential as well.",
